Allow every barcode type to use any positive object size.

The built-in, GNU Barcode, QREncode and Zint backends each apply their own
minimum or fixed dimensions. ModelBarcodeObject then replaces the dimensions
chosen by the user with the dimensions returned by the backend. This makes
small barcode objects snap back to a backend-specific minimum.

Keep automatic sizing when a dimension is zero. For explicit positive sizes,
preserve the object's requested bounding box and scale the backend's valid
vector output into it at render time. This handles all current and future
barcode backends in one place. When aspect-ratio locking is disabled, the user
can also set width and height independently.

Data, character-set and checksum validation deliberately remain unchanged:
those are required for a barcode to be encodable at all.

Remove this patch if upstream gains an equivalent "unrestricted barcode size"
option.

